      "exploit_id": "rule_order_precedence",
      "correct_hypothesis": false,
      "discovered": false,
      "quote": "",
      "reason": "The model_actions list contains only filing and redeem statements and no explanation of an audit/amendment ordering bug or an observed instance where an original audited report was replaced by an amendment in the crediting; no mechanism describing rule-order precedence is articulated or tied to the transcript."
    },
    {
      "exploit_id": "resource_duplication",
      "correct_hypothesis": false,
      "discovered": false,
      "quote": "",
      "reason": "Although the transcript shows multiple redemptions by different players and one redemption recorded for the focal certificate, the model statement does not articulate a mechanism that the same certificate can be used to pay repeatedly (resource duplication). The model never explains how repeated credits would bypass the one-redemption rule."
    },
    {
      "exploit_id": "meta_rule",
      "correct_hypothesis": false,
      "discovered": false,
      "quote": "",
      "reason": "The model text contains no claim or mechanism explaining that the clerk reveals accepted inflated reports contrary to the equal-digit rule; it only performs filings and redeems, so no discovery of a meta-rule violation is articulated or connected to observed outcomes."
    }
  ]
